{"type":"standard","title":"Teshenawa language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Teshenawa language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3436597","titles":{"canonical":"Teshenawa_language","normalized":"Teshenawa language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Teshenawa language</span></span>"},"pageid":16002162,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1332894251","tid":"fee7ded1-f149-11f0-a24a-56b0b51b1c75","timestamp":"2026-01-14T13:07:36Z","description":"Extinct Afro-Asiatic language of Nigeria","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teshenawa_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teshenawa_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teshenawa_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Teshenawa_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teshenawa_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Teshenawa_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teshenawa_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Teshenawa_language"}},"extract":"Teshenawa (Teshenanchi) is an extinct Afro-Asiatic language formerly spoken in Teshena town of Kafin Hausa LGA, Jigawa State, Nigeria. It was closely related to the also-extinct Auyokawa and still-living Bade.","extract_html":"<p><b>Teshenawa</b> (Teshenanchi) is an extinct Afro-Asiatic language formerly spoken in Teshena town of Kafin Hausa LGA, Jigawa State, Nigeria. It was closely related to the also-extinct Auyokawa and still-living Bade.</p>"}